       "text": "I've entered the order as you wrote it: **ibuprofen 1600 mg by mouth, four times daily**. The order ID is ORD-0001.\n\nThe order note says the dose is above usual limits (6400 mg/day, compared with a usual maximum of 3200 mg/day and 800 mg per dose). It says you confirmed the order as written and no clinical reason was given. It also asks pharmacy to verify before dispensing, so they'll probably contact you.\n\nAt this dose, it's worth keeping an eye on kidney function, signs of GI bleeding and blood pressure. You might also consider GI protection, such as a PPI. If this was meant to be a weight-based high-dose regimen, the usual schedule is twice daily, not four times. I can change the order or add your reason to the note if you'd like."
